      "title": "Metrics are incomplete after the current regeneration",
      "finding": "Scene reports contain all 842 rendered-view records and all 391 current paths, but only V55 and Superhawk metrics retain renderedViews: 71 and 28. The other 18 metrics files are empty, so only 42/391 current paths are represented in metrics. Quality records are current and internally hashed (370/370 paths and screenshot hashes; 20/20 manifest/master hashes), but quality evidence cannot repair the missing metrics evidence.",
      "requiredAction": "Regenerate metrics for all 20 selected IDs from the settled current render batch, verify 842 rendered views and 391 current-path references, and rerun this audit without changing production assets or quality records during the audit."
    },
    {
      "id": "VIS-001",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Reference-faithful geometry remains unproven",
      "finding": "The current fleet has 284 boxes, 48 cylinders, 78 decks, 44 chamfered boxes and 21 hull components, but collection-scale review still shows a repeated slab-hull/superstructure vocabulary. Draft distinctive-features checks fail for all 20.",
      "requiredAction": "Refine hulls, glazing, rooflines, decks and model-specific features against each reference dossier, then re-review the current canonical views."
    },
    {
      "id": "VIS-002",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Rooms are visible but remain blockout assemblies",
      "finding": "The room-camera clipping seen in audit 06 was not confirmed in the current 111 room frames, and all current room/deck frames are luminance-usable. However, all 20 room sets remain sparse cutaway assemblies dominated by beds, partitions, benches, cylinders and simple equipment rather than complete shells, joinery, fixtures and supported fittings. V55 room/deck frames are no longer blank, but its main/lower deck evidence remains furniture-like and does not establish deck fidelity.",
      "requiredAction": "Complete room enclosures, joinery, machinery, fixtures and physical supports; make every V55 deck view genuinely deck-specific; then rerun furnished-room, intersection, support and camera checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "VIS-003",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Material payloads remain visually insufficient",
      "finding": "All 84 GLBs contain material, texture and image payloads, but the parsed payload remains 806 materials, 650 textures and 650 32x32 images. Current frames still read primarily as flat color-block treatments, and the synchronized draft records fail textures and materials-in-all-views for all 20.",
      "requiredAction": "Use model-appropriate, sufficiently resolved materials and demonstrate consistent material treatment across every canonical current view."
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-001",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "One interior LOD pair is still unchanged",
      "finding": "The LOD pass now reduces triangles for all 20 exterior pairs and 21/22 interior pairs. Superhawk interior-main remains unchanged at 3904 -> 3904 triangles and is byte-identical; technical visual review remains pending for every ID.",
      "requiredAction": "Produce and visually validate a genuinely lighter Superhawk interior-main LOD, then rerun parsed LOD checks and technical visual review."
    },
    {
      "id": "APP-001",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "No independent approval exists",
      "finding": "All 20 quality records remain changes-required with reviewer independent-qa-pending. All technical visual reviews are pending, publicationReady is false for all 20, metrics self-review is not QA-approved for all 20, and the draft nine-check fail set remains present on every record even where the current visual pass improved camera and luminance evidence.",
      "requiredAction": "After metrics, geometry, rooms, materials and LOD blockers are fixed, run a new independent QA pass and record explicit approval per selected ID."
    }
